       1..n. Build the flattened sequence of n^2 pixels (1 of color_1, 3 of color_2, etc.).
    4. Place pyramids bottom-aligned at rows [H-n, H-1] -- this is the output.
    5. For each column, scatter its n^2 pixels into distinct rows of that column,
       all above row H-n (strict). Rows chosen randomly with gaps >= 0; order preserved.
    6. Clear the pyramid region to get the input grid.

